# Audit the roadmap against the results

Document ID: `reiyah.roadmap-audit`. Version: `0.1.0`.
Lifecycle status: `exploratory`. As of 19 September 2026.

**The research followed its falsification plan; the product advantage has not
been demonstrated. The navigation needs updating.** The strongest next direction
is to make a consequential revision decision with qualified observations and
measured costs, while comparing against modern statistical auditing as well as
the existing exact methods. This is a research recommendation, not evidence that
Reiyah is state of the art or that its strategy is globally optimal.

The [current roadmap](../../../docs/ENGINE_ROADMAP_2026-09-19.md) replaces the
September 13 roadmap and September 17 mission as current navigation. Historical
documents, frozen experiments and their negative results remain intact. The
operator assigned this audit and continuing Reiyah research to one Codex session;
the former Engine/Fable division is no longer the current ownership arrangement.

## Did execution follow the plan?

The audit selects main `23db0b322707e7e3d2e93efbb33d4e0127070c47`.
[audit.json](audit.json) binds the inspected local artifacts to exact bytes.
The five numbered obligations come from the
[September 17 mission](../../../docs/REIYAH_NEXT_MISSION_2026-09-17.md).

| Obligation | What the retained evidence establishes | Audit decision |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1. Finish the common proof boundary | Matching, endpoint, component, linear, replacement and observation-applicability checks exist. Their finite scope and work limits are recorded. | Delivered for the declared families; no universal proof of program correctness or reference truth. |
| 2. Run the competitive development benchmark | The [first four-arm study](../../value-disproof/0.1.0/README.md) and [qualified public-output study](../../public-predictions/0.1.0/README.md) were executed. Equal selectors and mathematics give equal conventional/native query histories. The latter baseline attains all 99 resolved retrospective query floors; the alternative wins on zero cases and loses on four. | Delivered with negative evidence for a selector/stopping advantage. Retire further tuning on these resolved contracts. |
| 3. Freeze a prospective external test | The public-output experiment has freezes and qualified exposed inputs. All 1,433 reserved images remain closed. Previously exposed development inputs are not a distinct held-out confirmation. | A prospective external value test remains unrun; do not promote the development freezes into one. |
| 4. Measure changed-system reuse | Applicability checking exists. The small certificate-reuse assay was slower than recomputation. Two publisher generations are not genuine customer revision history; human and complete economic costs are unknown. | Software capability delivered; practical reuse benefit unestablished. |
| 5. Expand only after a consequential win | Insertion, geometry, timing and operating-policy studies exposed limits of the perception contract. No new domain or product deployment follows. | Semantic stress tests were warranted; platform/domain expansion remains unearned. |
| Keep every failure and unresolved result | [Cost/outcome reconciliation](../../mission-costs/0.1.0/OUTCOMES.md) and the [final timing study](../../operating-timing-witness/0.1.0/OUTCOMES.md) retain failures, corrections, blocked members and conflicting worlds. | Evidence discipline preserved. No failure is converted to an empty or successful observation. |
| Demonstrate demand and full workflow value | The [existing workflow brief](../../value-disproof/0.1.0/WORKFLOW_BRIEF.md) specifies required evidence; it is not a customer conversation. | Unmeasured. Five accounts and two team comparisons remain acquisition targets. |
| Advance the original HARBOR constructs | The [scientific charter](../../../docs/SCIENTIFIC_CHARTER.md) concerns belief, readiness, recovery, joint misses, causal effects, transfer and worst groups. Present perception certificates validate none of those by analogy. | The current application is narrower than the program. Those constructs need their own observation and identification protocols. |

This distinguishes scientific progress from commercial progress. Finding that a
competent baseline already attains the query floor is successful falsification of
that proposed advantage. It is not a product win, nor proof that every possible
Reiyah application has no value.

## Reconcile the latest result

The published timing CSV contains **7,707 dependent rows**: 642 supported,
3,076 excluded, 1,790 unresolved and 2,199 input-blocked. All 1,790 unresolved
rows now have checked opposing worlds. The last 279 evidence gaps closed without
changing any decision, universal bound, cutoff or population. The 279 target
rows share 356 filtered states and 397 state/contract pairs. These are not 279
independent decisions or customer problems.

This audit recounts the public CSV and checks its recorded digest, summary and
source bindings. It does not rerun the closed search, reopen images or call its
own readback independent scientific verification. The existing result that all
89 new searches reached both universal endpoints remains conditional on those
specific operands, rather than exhaustive search of arbitrary rectangles.

Three concrete navigation defects need correction:

1. The September 13 roadmap still describes the next selector comparison and
   separate owners. Both are superseded by later results and operator instructions.
2. The September 17 mission's next competitive development experiment has run.
   Repeating its task list without the parity result would misdirect effort.
3. Workflow brief 0.1.10 still describes 279 timing attainability gaps. Those gaps
   are now closed. Its owner/interview questions remain useful; its dated result
   paragraph is historical. Keep using that brief with this correction rather
   than creating another empty customer inventory.

The new roadmap, README entry and current handoff supply the correction without
rewriting the closed artifacts. The old frontier baseline remains a dated,
pointer-only review; this packet provides a separately retained comparison for
the current decision-assurance question.

## What the frontier review changes

[FRONTIER.md](FRONTIER.md) evaluates 20 selected primary works. Thirteen have
retained full HTML with relevant sections inspected; seven are explicitly limited
to the publisher/author abstract record. The search includes 2026 papers and
foundational comparators. [METHOD.md](METHOD.md) records selection, search limits,
review depth and failures; [sources.json](sources.json) binds versions, dates,
authors, access and redistribution status to retained private bytes.

The consequential changes are to include weighted sequential audits among the
baselines; separate statistical guarantees from exact conditional certificates;
test model-assisted evaluation against a labels-only alternative; and keep
measurement validity and downstream consequences outside a matching proof's claim.
Recent work reinforces these boundaries. It does not supply missing observations,
prove Reiyah's economics or establish novelty for the proposed combination.

